# Files another tool owns and rewrites.
#
# `format:check` globs every yaml in the repo, which catches the lockfile — and prettier's
# preferred layout is not pnpm's. Formatting it once makes CI pass until the next `pnpm add`
# rewrites it, and then the failure returns looking unrelated to whatever that change was. It
# has never actually been prettier-clean; CI simply had no remote to run against until now.
#
# A lockfile is generated, reviewed as a diff rather than read, and owned by the package
# manager. Prettier has no business in it.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Build output. Not matched by the current glob, but listed so it stays that way if the glob
# ever widens — a bundled file has no style to check.
packages/adapter/dist/
